<title>JAPAN: LTCB reveals problem loans.</title>
<headline>LTCB reveals problem loans.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Long-Term Credit Bank of Japan Ltd has disclosed its restructured loans (in billions of yen unless specified):</p>
<p>					end-Sep 96     end-Mar 96</p>
<p>  Restructured loans	    19.04	   257.17</p>
<p>  Bad loans			351.09	   106.54</p>
<p>  Non-performing loans	 680.45	    671.7</p>
<p>  Loans to troubled clients  170.37	   161.52</p>
<p>  Total problem loans	    1.22 trln	 1.2 trln</p>
<p>Restructured loans are those on which interest rates have been cut to help corporate restructuring. Bad loans are to bankrupt firms and non-performing are those with interest payments in arrears by six months or more. Loans to troubled clients are mainly to the bank's non-bank affiliates.</p>
</text>
